body:
Hi,

I couldn't create a simple test case to reproduce the issue, but I believe I have identified where it occurs:

In `js/modules/k6/browser/k6ext/promise.go`, you have this code:

```go
func promise(ctx context.Context, fn PromisifiedFunc) *sobek.Promise {
	p, resolve, reject := promises.New(GetVU(ctx))
	go func() {
		v, err := fn()
		if err != nil {
			reject(err)
			return
		}
		resolve(v)
	}()

	return p
}
```

There is a race condition where the parent goroutine and its child share the same `Runtime` object, allowing both to access the internal VM object concurrently. Since both are modifying the stack simultaneously, this leads to index/pointer issues.

Attached file is an example from one of my run with the `-race` flag being used

